+/* Physical T12 handset on CAN2; steering/drive controllers remain on CAN1.
+ * 0x10A: byte2 A = enable (nonzero active), byte3 B = ignored.
+ * A rising edge requests power on; while active, switch frames retry acquiring
+ * a zero-target shared session. Joystick frames renew and submit targets.
+ * A falling edge stops this handset's session. Power is switched off after
+ * 3000 ms only if this module originally switched it on; A on cancels the delay.
+ * 0x10B: byte0-1 = steering int16, byte4-5 = throttle int16.
+ * Switch and joystick streams must both remain fresh. Every shared safety
+ * gate (calibration, feedback, reversal, Bus-Off, OTA and lease) still applies.
+ * Power command state is not a measurement of physical supply readiness. */
 
